**Changed**

  - Updated dependencies


[0.9.0] - 2026-05-18
====================

**Changed**

  - ``scaldys.toml`` renamed to ``scaldys-project.toml``.  All references
    updated across code, documentation, and packaging scripts:
    ``packaging/windows/scaldys-template.iss``,
    ``docs/developer_guide/`` (``.rst`` files), and ``README.md``.


[0.8.0] - 2026-05-18
====================

**Changed**

  - ``release.yml``: automated PyPI publishing removed.  The workflow now
    only creates a GitHub Release with auto-generated notes when a ``v*`` tag
    is pushed.  PyPI publishing is handled manually via
    ``scaldys-project publish`` (see below).

    Rationale: ``uv build`` on a CI runner produces a pure-Python wheel that
    exposes Cython source code on PyPI.  The correct artifact — a binary wheel
    with compiled ``.pyd`` extensions — can only be produced by the local
    ``scaldys-project build all`` pipeline.

  - ``ci.yml``: ``build`` job removed.  CI now covers only quality gates:
    lint (``ruff check``), format check (``ruff format --diff``), type
    checking (``pyright``), and tests (``pytest --cov``) across Ubuntu,
    macOS, and Windows.  The ``build`` job produced a pure-Python wheel that
    was never used, adding noise and masking the true release artifact.

**Docs**

  - ``docs/developer_guide/``: *Publishing* guide rewritten for the new
    release workflow.  Explains why manual publishing is required for
    binary-wheel projects, documents the ``scaldys-project publish`` command
    and its guard-rails (rejects pure-Python wheels, rejects multiple binary
    wheels), covers PyPI API token setup, and provides a TestPyPI dry-run
    checklist.  The previous OIDC Trusted Publishing content has been removed
    as it is no longer applicable.


